External-provider fallback decision record (M6)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

M6 considered an external-provider inference fallback (OpenAI / Bedrock / etc.)
that would forward user prompts to a third-party API when in-cluster GPU
capacity is unavailable.

Decision: NOT implemented; will not be implemented in any future milestone
          without explicit maintainer review.

Rationale:
- The platform's stance per AGENTS.md is "self-hosted, organization-private,
  maintainer-controlled, not a shared multi-tenant SaaS".  An implicit
  external fallback would materially change the data-privacy posture.
- The observability content policy (docs/07-observability.md) explicitly
  forbids prompt/completion content in any telemetry surface; an external
  fallback would create a third-party data flow that conflicts with that
  posture absent a separate reviewed policy.

What we ship instead:
- Aggressive in-cluster elasticity via Karpenter on spot capacity.
- Honest 503 + Retry-After responses on capacity shortage (already in M4).
- Optional warm-pool replica in production (configured per-environment).
- Per-environment HPA tuning on vLLM queue depth.

See docs/09-scaling-policy.md for the full degraded-mode response policy.

