M11 sandbox-design sign-off
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

M11 build task 1 requires a tool-execution sandbox design reviewed and signed
off by a maintainer before implementation (AGENTS.md escalation trigger).

Design: docs/m11-sandbox-design.md (first increment — declarative, allow-listed
tools run out-of-process with a scrubbed environment, RLIMIT CPU/memory/FSIZE
limits, wall-clock timeout with SIGKILL, deny-by-default per-tenant allow-list,
operator kill-switch, per-tenant rate/concurrency limits, and content-policy
audit logging).

Sign-off: approved by the maintainer for the first increment. Arbitrary
shell/command execution, network-egress tools, filesystem-writing tools, and
cloud-credential access remain EXCLUDED by default and require a separate,
stronger sandbox (Kubernetes Job + NetworkPolicy deny-egress + read-only
rootfs) with its own review before adoption.

Provenance: tool-schema / tool-parsing / tool-result patterns are adapted
(structural conventions only) from common agent-tooling designs; no third-party
agent framework is vendored. The optional "deep-research" sub-feature (which
would adapt actual Apache-2.0 upstream code) is NOT adopted in this increment
and would require its own decision record + the Apache-2.0 attribution
checkpoint in the M11 instruction file.

